+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GuN7Abr6c89hY15zv8yrfb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Reactive Spreadsheet Engine\n2\t\n3\tBuild a spreadsheet engine as a TypeScript library. The engine manages a grid of cells that can contain values or formulas, with automatic reactive updates when dependencies change.\n4\t\n5\t## Cell References\n6\t\n7\tCells are referenced by column letter(s) followed by a row number: `A1`, `B2`, `Z100`, `AA1`, etc. Columns use letters A-Z, then AA-AZ, BA-BZ, etc. Rows are 1-based integers.\n8\t\n9\t## Cell Values\n10\t\n11\tA cell can contain:\n12\t- **Numbers**: `42`, `3.14`\n13\t- **Strings**: `\"hello\"` (text values)\n14\t- **Booleans**: `true`, `false`\n15\t- **Formulas**: expressions starting with `=` (e.g., `=A1+B1`, `=SUM(A1:A5)`)\n16\t\n17\t## Formulas\n18\t\n19\tFormulas begin with `=` and support:\n20\t- **Arithmetic operators**: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`\n21\t- **Parentheses** for grouping: `=(A1+B1)*2`\n22\t- **Cell references**: `=A1`, `=B2+C3`\n23\t- **Comparison operators**: `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`, `=`, `<>` (used in IF conditions)\n24\t\n25\t## Built-in Functions\n26\t\n27\t- `SUM(range)` — sum of all numeric values in the range\n28\t- `AVERAGE(range)` — arithmetic mean of numeric values in the range\n29\t- `MIN(range)` — smallest numeric value in the range\n30\t- `MAX(range)` — largest numeric value in the range\n31\t- `COUNT(range)` — count of numeric values in the range\n32\t- `IF(condition, trueValue, falseValue)` — conditional expression\n33\t\n34\t## Ranges\n35\t\n36\tRanges are specified as `start:end`:\n37\t- **Column range**: `A1:A5` — cells A1, A2, A3, A4, A5\n38\t- **Row range**: `A1:C1` — cells A1, B1, C1\n39\t- **Block range**: `A1:C3` — all cells in the 2D rectangle from A1 to C3\n40\t\n41\t## Reactive Updates\n42\t\n43\tWhen a cell's value changes, all cells that depend on it (directly or transitively) must automatically recompute. For example, if `B1` contains `=A1+1` and `A1` changes from `5` to `10`, then `B1` should automatically update from `6` to `11`.\n44\t\n45\t## Circular Reference Detection\n46\t\n47\tIf setting a cell would create a circular dependency (e.g., `A1=B1` and `B1=A1`), the engine must detect this and throw an error. This includes indirect cycles through any number of intermediate cells.\n48\t\n49\t## API\n50\t\n51\tExport a `Spreadsheet` class (or equivalent) from `src/index.ts` with the following interface:\n52\t\n53\t```typescript\n54\tclass Spreadsheet {\n55\t  // Set a cell's value. Can be a raw value or a formula string starting with '='\n56\t  set(cell: string, value: string | number | boolean): void;\n57\t\n58\t  // Get a cell's computed value. Returns null for empty cells.\n59\t  get(cell: string): string | number | boolean | null;\n60\t\n61\t  // Get the display string for a cell's computed value.\n62\t  getDisplay(cell: string): string;\n63\t\n64\t  // Get all non-empty cells as a Map from cell reference to computed value.\n65\t  getCells(): Map<string, any>;\n66\t}\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\t## Example Usage\n70\t\n71\t```typescript\n72\tconst sheet = new Spreadsheet();\n73\t\n74\tsheet.set('A1', 10);\n75\tsheet.set('A2', 20);\n76\tsheet.set('A3', '=A1+A2');\n77\tsheet.get('A3');        // 30\n78\tsheet.getDisplay('A3'); // \"30\"\n79\t\n80\tsheet.set('A1', 50);\n81\tsheet.get('A3');        // 70  (reactively updated)\n82\t\n83\tsheet.set('B1', '=SUM(A1:A2)');\n84\tsheet.get('B1');        // 70\n85\t\n86\tsheet.set('C1', '=IF(A1>30, \"big\", \"small\")');\n87\tsheet.get('C1');        // \"big\"\n88\t```\n89\t\n90\t## Requirements\n91\t\n92\t- Implement in TypeScript with proper types\n93\t- Export from `src/index.ts`\n94\t- Write tests using Vitest\n95\t- All code in the `src/` directory\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb3f5de4-3e53-494c-a8d3-c3c40190c42b","uuid":"877b0e96-e8ce-429f-99fe-1d8b749ffc86","timestamp":"2026-05-29T08:35:12.383Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/TASK.md","content":"# Reactive Spreadsheet Engine\n\nBuild a spreadsheet engine as a TypeScript library. The engine manages a grid of cells that can contain values or formulas, with automatic reactive updates when dependencies change.\n\n## Cell References\n\nCells are referenced by column letter(s) followed by a row number: `A1`, `B2`, `Z100`, `AA1`, etc. Columns use letters A-Z, then AA-AZ, BA-BZ, etc. Rows are 1-based integers.\n\n## Cell Values\n\nA cell can contain:\n- **Numbers**: `42`, `3.14`\n- **Strings**: `\"hello\"` (text values)\n- **Booleans**: `true`, `false`\n- **Formulas**: expressions starting with `=` (e.g., `=A1+B1`, `=SUM(A1:A5)`)\n\n## Formulas\n\nFormulas begin with `=` and support:\n- **Arithmetic operators**: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`\n- **Parentheses** for grouping: `=(A1+B1)*2`\n- **Cell references**: `=A1`, `=B2+C3`\n- **Comparison operators**: `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`, `=`, `<>` (used in IF conditions)\n\n## Built-in Functions\n\n- `SUM(range)` — sum of all numeric values in the range\n- `AVERAGE(range)` — arithmetic mean of numeric values in the range\n- `MIN(range)` — smallest numeric value in the range\n- `MAX(range)` — largest numeric value in the range\n- `COUNT(range)` — count of numeric values in the range\n- `IF(condition, trueValue, falseValue)` — conditional expression\n\n## Ranges\n\nRanges are specified as `start:end`:\n- **Column range**: `A1:A5` — cells A1, A2, A3, A4, A5\n- **Row range**: `A1:C1` — cells A1, B1, C1\n- **Block range**: `A1:C3` — all cells in the 2D rectangle from A1 to C3\n\n## Reactive Updates\n\nWhen a cell's value changes, all cells that depend on it (directly or transitively) must automatically recompute. For example, if `B1` contains `=A1+1` and `A1` changes from `5` to `10`, then `B1` should automatically update from `6` to `11`.\n\n## Circular Reference Detection\n\nIf setting a cell would create a circular dependency (e.g., `A1=B1` and `B1=A1`), the engine must detect this and throw an error. This includes indirect cycles through any number of intermediate cells.\n\n## API\n\nExport a `Spreadsheet` class (or equivalent) from `src/index.ts` with the following interface:\n\n```typescript\nclass Spreadsheet {\n  // Set a cell's value. Can be a raw value or a formula string starting with '='\n  set(cell: string, value: string | number | boolean): void;\n\n  // Get a cell's computed value. Returns null for empty cells.\n  get(cell: string): string | number | boolean | null;\n\n  // Get the display string for a cell's computed value.\n  getDisplay(cell: string): string;\n\n  // Get all non-empty cells as a Map from cell reference to computed value.\n  getCells(): Map<string, any>;\n}\n```\n\n## Example Usage\n\n```typescript\nconst sheet = new Spreadsheet();\n\nsheet.set('A1', 10);\nsheet.set('A2', 20);\nsheet.set('A3', '=A1+A2');\nsheet.get('A3');        // 30\nsheet.getDisplay('A3'); // \"30\"\n\nsheet.set('A1', 50);\nsheet.get('A3');        // 70  (reactively updated)\n\nsheet.set('B1', '=SUM(A1:A2)');\nsheet.get('B1');        // 70\n\nsheet.set('C1', '=IF(A1>30, \"big\", \"small\")');\nsheet.get('C1');        // \"big\"\n```\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Implement in TypeScript with proper types\n- Export from `src/index.ts`\n- Write tests using Vitest\n- All code in the `src/` directory\n","numLines":96,"startLine":1,"totalLines":96}}}
